OL,4,CPROGRAMMES
OL,5,
OL,6,CG1984FThe Old Man of Hoy airs on BBC
OL,7,FOne.
OL,8,
OL,9,FRadio Times: "Live coverage of an
OL,10,Fattempt by four climbers on the most
OL,11,Ffamous chunk of rock in Britain. It's
OL,12,F17 years since Hoy was televised but
OL,13,Fthe risks haven't diminished.
OL,14,
OL,15,F"Murray Hamilton and Pete Whillance
OL,16,Fwill tackle the overhanging south-east
OL,17,Fedge, but without the protection of the
OL,18,Fbolts and pitons used on the first
OL,19,Fascent. The rock itself, Torridon
OL,20,Fsandstone, has a tendency to crumble
OL,21,Flike a digestive biscuit.
OL,22,
OL,23,Sppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
